A Stripe-shaped live-key string (`sk_live_` prefix) is committed directly into source. Even though the comment labels it a probe fixture and the value contains `ExAmPlE` markers, the prefix pattern will be caught by secret scanners and could be flagged as a real credential leak. A probe fixture testing the security lens should use a value that is unambiguously fake (e.g., `sk_test_` or a clearly non-Stripe-shaped string), or the file must be excluded from secret-scanning scope with a documented suppression. **Block-level risk if this file were ever pushed to a real repo without suppression.**

