### HIGH — Correctness

**`probe_fixture.py:22`** — `for i in range(n + 1):`

Off-by-one. `range(n + 1)` iterates indices `0..n` inclusive, so `items[n]` is accessed. For a caller passing `n = len(items)` (the natural "sum all" call), this raises `IndexError`. The docstring correctly documents the intended bound as `range(n)`. The bug as written means `sum_first_n([1, 2, 3], 3)` crashes rather than returning `6`.

